        "header": "3Method: TheStateful Harness",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.26811/2610.26811v1/fig1_final.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Counterfactual Pairs Reveal the Role of Hidden State.The two cases share the first frameI0I_{0}and actionata_{t}but differ in the hidden flaghas_key.\nIn the illustrated failure, an unwrapped video model opens the chest in both cases, violating the rule when no key is available.\nThe harness maintains semantic and spatial state, executes the shared rule to determine whether the chest remains locked or opens, and renders each outcome with the same frozen video model.",
                "position": 460
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.26811/2610.26811v1/fig2_final.png",
                "caption": "Figure 3:TheStateful Harness.InStage 0, a coding agent constructs an executable game definition specifying the state, actions, rules, events, goals, and visual semantics.\nInStage 1, the runtime evaluates the rules, updates the state, and determines the event and goal status for each action.\nThe resolved event is compiled into an instruction for the frozen video modelVθV_{\\theta}.\nVisual observations of the generated clip inform the state used in the next turn.\nAdaptation to a new game changes the game definition while retaining the shared runtime and video model weights.",
                "position": 538
            }
        ]
    },
